- if (!fp->fi_fds[O_RDONLY]) { fp->fi_fds[O_RDONLY] = nf; nf = NULL; } fp->fi_rdeleg_file = nfsd_file_get(fp->fi_fds[O_RDONLY]);
- if (nf) nfsd_file_put(nf);
- if (rnf) { nfsd_file_put(rnf); nfs4_file_put_access(fp, NFS4_SHARE_ACCESS_READ); }
Reason:
The first statement only assigns the new `nf` to `fp->fi_fds[O_RDONLY]` if the slot is empty, avoiding overwriting an existing reference. It then obtains a new reference via `nfsd_file_get()` for `fi_rdeleg_file`, properly incrementing the refcount. The second statement releases the newly acquired `nf` if it was not stored (i.e., if `fi_fds[O_RDONLY]` already existed). The third statement, in `put_deleg_file()`, now also calls `nfsd_file_put(rnf)` to release the explicit reference for `fi_rdeleg_file`, regardless of `fi_access` counters, ensuring the delegation's `nfsd_file` reference is always freed.

